---
import { profile } from '../../data/profile'
const updated = '31 October 2026'
---

<div class="content" data-app-content="privacy">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

  <p style="margin-top:18px">
    This is my personal portfolio. It is built to collect as little as possible. This page describes what the site does
    today; it will be updated before anything here changes.
  </p>

  <h2>What I collect</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing. The site has no accounts, no contact form, no analytics, no advertising and no tracking. It sets no
    cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>What your browser keeps on your device</h2>
  <p>
    A few small settings are stored in your own browser so the site works the way you left it. They never leave your
    device:
  </p>
  <ul class="points">
    <li>
      <strong>view</strong>: whether you chose the plain view instead of the desktop (kept until you clear it).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>campaign</strong>: which introduction to show if you arrived from a link with a campaign tag (cleared when
      you close the tab).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>recent-apps</strong>: the pages you opened, for the phone's Recent list (cleared when you close the tab).
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can remove them at any time by clearing this site's data in your browser settings.</p>

  <h2>Links with campaign tags</h2>
  <p>
    Some links to this site include tags such as <code>utm_campaign</code>. Your browser reads them only to choose which
    introduction to show. They are not stored anywhere else and are not sent to anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    Like any website, the company that hosts it may keep standard request logs (such as IP address, time and page
    requested) for security and to keep the service running. I don't use those logs to identify visitors.
  </p>

  <h2>Fonts and other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Fonts are served from this site, not from a third party. Links to GitHub and LinkedIn take you to those sites, and
    their own privacy policies apply there.
  </p>

  <h2>Coming later</h2>
  <p>
    I plan to add privacy-friendly, cookie-free visit statistics, a contact form and an assistant that answers questions
    about my work. Before any of them goes live, this page will explain what each one collects, why, how long it is kept
    and how to opt out.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions or requests about your data:{' '}
    {profile.email ? <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a> : 'see the contact page'}.
  </p>
</div>
